meta {
  name: Entity Ownership Tracing
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{aiUwLambdaUrl}}/workflows/entity-ownership-tracing/run
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "loan_id": {{loan_id}},
    "validation_id": "{{borrower_eligibility_validation_id}}",
    "workflow_run_id": "{{workflow_run_id_phase_1}}",
    "phase": "PHASE_1"
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  aiUwLambdaUrl: https://xsug4clelwjxmace3mckpnmdae0flkdi.lambda-url.us-east-1.on.aws
  borrower_eligibility_validation_id: aabdeb0e-2ea6-4a46-9524-cac9410bcefd
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Layered entity ownership tracer (workflows PR #40). Recursively traces the
  borrower's entity ownership down to the ultimate individual owners (UBOs)
  and flags the required guarantors per RBI's per-level >=20% rule.
  
  Routing:
    Bruno -> Function URL -> ai-uw-dispatcher -> ai-uw-borrower-eligibility
  
  Registered as `entity-ownership-tracing` in the dispatcher's
  WORKFLOW_ROUTING and in the borrower-eligibility handler REGISTRY. It is a
  standalone Phase 1 workflow — NOT part of the `phase1-borrower-eligibility`
  orchestrator — so it has to be triggered on its own.
  
  Body:
    loan_id          required
    validation_id    UUID of the BorrowerEligibilityValidation the traced
                     EntityOwner rows attach to. Optional but STRONGLY
                     recommended: when omitted the Lambda falls back to
                     GET /api/workflows/borrower-eligibility-validations/?loan_application_id=<loan_id>
                     and takes the first (latest, non-archived) row — which
                     silently attaches the owners to a PREVIOUS run if the new
                     validation does not exist yet. The call still returns 200,
                     so the mistake is invisible.
    workflow_run_id  optional — used for the phase-result callback
    model            optional — overrides the extraction model
  
  `loan_documents` / `loan_application_form` are hydrated automatically via
  load_loan_context; do not send them. The borrower entity name is read from
  the loan application form (`result.formData.entity_name`); without it the
  workflow returns
  {"status": "error", "error": "borrower entity_name not found in loan application"}.
  
  One AI extraction runs per entity document (Operating Agreement / Articles /
  EIN), so this is slow — trigger it and read the persisted rows rather than
  waiting on the response body:
    GET /api/workflows/entity-owners/?borrower_eligibility_validation=<id>
    GET /api/workflows/entity-owners/?parent_owner=<owner_id>
  
  Response fields worth checking:
    status                       PASS, or REVIEW when the borrower doc is
                                 missing or a high-severity condition fired
    validation_id                the id actually used — verify it is the one
                                 you expected
    entity_owner_rows_created    0 means nothing was persisted
    required_guarantors          individuals reached via a fully-qualifying
                                 >=20% chain
    ultimate_individual_owners   leaf individuals (UBOs)
    conditions                   missing docs, foreign-entity due diligence,
                                 low-confidence matches, manual review
    layered_structure_detected   true when any direct owner of the borrower is
                                 itself an entity
}
